<h3>What the registry does not list</h3>

<p>Correction to an earlier research note: that note said the registry's annual registrations would list officers or members. For an LLC they do not. The Secretary of State's own questions-and-answers page says "members or managers for LLCs are not listed" (the source checker's read through a fetch tool; the page refuses a plain request). An amendment can be signed by a member or manager, by an organizer where the company has no members or managers, or by an attorney-in-fact. So the June 15, 2026 amendment, if obtained, can establish the name change, its date, and who signed in what stated capacity. It cannot by itself show who owns the company, or whether ownership changed.</p>

<p>The source adds, as a general description and not legal advice: ownership of a company and title to its land are different things. A federal bankruptcy court opinion read by the source checker (N.D. Ga., March 31, 2021, describing Georgia's LLC statute, O.C.G.A. 14-11-501) states that members have no interest in specific property of the LLC. So a transfer of the interests in an LLC need not involve any deed, and the deed index may show nothing even if control of the company changed. An operating agreement, and any purchase, option, loan or joint-venture contract between private parties, is not routinely public.</p>

<h2>What a Party Says</h2>

<p>Two statements, set side by side and not reconciled. Each is a claim by a party. Neither was checked against a deed.</p>

<table class="report-table">
<thead>
<tr>
<th>June 16, 2026: Renewal Development Group LLC, in its press release on PR Newswire</th>
<th>June 29, 2026: an Abebe Ventures representative, as printed by Urbanize Atlanta</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>"The property was previously owned by entities affiliated with Mekonen (Mike) Abebe and we acknowledge his prior engagement in the project's conceptualization. Renewal Development Group and its affiliated ownership entities now own and control the project and will be responsible for all future development, investment, and implementation activities."</td>
<td>"The article states that Renewal Development Group has taken over ownership and control of the properties from Abebe Ventures. This is factually incorrect as it pertains to the following parcels: 1313 Sylvan Road SW; 1215 Sylvan Road SW; 984, 985, and 997 Cox Ave. SW. Mr. Abebe remains the owner of record of each of these properties."</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/renewal-development-group-celebrates-atlanta-city-council-approval-of-transformational-sylvan-road-redevelopment-302801061.html" target="_blank">Renewal's release</a>; <a href="https://atlanta.urbanize.city/post/sylvan-southwest-atl-3000-home-project-beltline-approval-city-images" target="_blank">Urbanize Atlanta, June 17, 2026, updated June 29</a>.</p>

<p>The June 29 statement is printed inside the June 17 Urbanize article as an update note, "UPDATE: 7:24 p.m., June 29: An Abebe Ventures representative sends the following". It answers this sentence by the reporter: "Renewal Development Group has taken over ownership and control of the property in question from Atlanta-based Abebe Ventures, which originated the Sylvan Road concept last year." It is a statement received and printed, inside the article. No separate correction article was found.</p>

<p>Renewal's release also says: "Renewal Development Group controls approximately 45 acres of strategically located development land in Atlanta". No address other than Sylvan Road is given. The release does not state where the company is formed or registered. It is the only Renewal release found on that service, and no Renewal statement from 2023, 2024 or 2025 about its dealings with Abebe entities was found.</p>

<p>The Abebe Ventures page abebe.com/sylvan-rd, read October 7, 2026, describes "A transformative mixed-use development that would bring about 3,032 residential units ... along Sylvan Road in Capitol View." The word "Renewal" does not occur on it.</p>

<p>In the statements read, no party and no reporter says there is a quarrel, a breach or a suit between the two sides. No statement found uses the words purchase, joint venture, loan, option or membership interest for anything between the two sides.</p>

